@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- Figures this row takes from the National Insurance Institute's own publications, because the Law
-- states the rule that produces them but not the figure. Each carries the URL, the retrieval time
-- (UTC) and the sha256 of the bytes fetched. The pages were fetched with curl on 2026-10-06 directly
-- (not through the proxy) and are not deposited (the site reserves its rights); NOTES.md section 7
-- transcribes what each says. The site describes its content as general information and not the
-- binding text of the Law, so each figure here is an official publication of a computed amount, not
-- law. The rules that make the figures are in s 1 (the basic amount, the average wage), s 2 (the
-- average wage for contributions), s 334(a) (the threshold) and the Minimum Wage Law; none of those
-- is in this row.
--
-- The first three names are row IL-04's, for the same three figures (its
-- nii-il04-published-figures.l4); the bytes this row fetched have different sha256s from IL-04's
-- fetch of the same pages, as the pages are generated on each request, and print the same figures.
-- Figures used only as test expectations (the Institute's printed minimum income and the
-- contributions it prints for those with no income) are in the tests module, with provenance.

§ `Figures published by the National Insurance Institute`

§§ `The reduced collection threshold for 2026`

-- s 334(a); used here by s 342(f)(2) and in the tests. "on monthly income up to 7,703 NIS (reduced
-- rate)", and "(from 01.01.2026)", on the rates pages for employees and for the self-employed:
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%d7%9c%d7%a2%d7%95%d7%91%d7%93%d7%99%d7%9d%20%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%99%d7%9d.aspx
--     14:49:54Z, sha256 34ade94d9f315ad684979636e7b3d1e166cb09bf676b1ea1a20f4d82fa242c7b
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%d7%9c%d7%a2%d7%a6%d7%9e%d7%90%d7%99%d7%9d.aspx
--     14:49:42Z, sha256 5d1e1a490b11bb63f1430677185a977045a173d32cde6fca5317836a34827567
@ref National Insurance Institute, rates pages for employees and for the self-employed, fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 334(a) (source line 3605)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 7_703

§§ `The average wage from 1 January 2026`

-- The Institute publishes the average wage "under section 1" and "under section 2", each "for
-- benefits" and "for contributions". From 01.01.2026: 13,566 under section 1 and 13,769 under
-- section 2, each for contributions as for benefits; the page lists no later update in 2026.
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a8%20%d7%9e%d7%9e%d7%95%d7%a6%d7%a2.aspx
--     14:49:57Z, sha256 0afd95b65113a99dfc9bb9cd277090a927d26fa0c39b49a75be4ec1931829532
-- The consolidation's editorial notes give the same two figures (aids, not authority):
-- src:226 | [note: השכר הממוצע לפי הגדרה זאת: בשנת 2026, 13,566 ש״ח.]
-- src:233 | [note: נכון לשנת 2026, השכר הממוצע המדוד הוא 13,769 ש״ח.]
-- Which of the two Schedule K reads is NOTES.md fork F1.
@ref National Insurance Institute, "average wage under sections 1 and 2", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 1 "השכר הממוצע" (source lines 222-226)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage from 1 January 2026 under section 1, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 13_566

@ref National Insurance Institute, "average wage under sections 1 and 2", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 2(b) (source lines 236-238)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage from 1 January 2026 as calculated under section 2, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 13_769

§§ `The basic amount under paragraph (3), from 1 January 2026`

-- Schedule K's "basic amount" is the one in paragraph (3) of the s 1 definition: 6,964 NIS "nominal
-- for 2005", updated each 1 January by the rise in the consumer price index. The Institute's table
-- of basic amounts prints, from 1.01.2026, "basic amount 3, for updating benefits not updated by
-- basic amounts 1, 2 and 4, and for computing the maximum income for collecting contributions":
-- 10,382 (a change of 2.4%; 10,139 from 1.01.2025).
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%94%d7%a1%d7%9b%d7%95%d7%9d%20%d7%94%d7%91%d7%a1%d7%99%d7%a1%d7%99%20%d7%9c%d7%97%d7%99%d7%a9%d7%95%d7%91%20%d7%a7%d7%a6%d7%91%d7%90%d7%95%d7%aa.aspx
--     14:52:50Z, sha256 c585c6469d5c358d0230523208b54b6501ad624b06775eed2235f52bdc0a13d9
-- The consolidation's editorial note gives the same figure (an aid):
-- src:191 | (3) לענין כל גמלה שאינה מנויה בפסקאות (1) או (2) – 6,964 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2005 בשנת 2025, 10,139 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 10,382 ש״ח)];
@ref National Insurance Institute, "the basic amount for computing benefits", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" (3) (source line 191)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount under paragraph (3) from 1 January 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 10_382

§§ `The monthly minimum wage`

-- The Institute's minimum wage page, "minimum wage from age 18 and over": monthly wage 6,443.85 NIS
-- "(from 01.04.2026)"; in its table, 6,247.67 from 01.04.2025. So for the first months of the four
-- quarters of 2026: January 6,247.67; April, July and October 6,443.85. These are the full monthly
-- minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over; the figure Schedule K reads is the one "applicable to a
-- particular employee", which for a part-time employee is the partial minimum wage (fork F11).
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a8%20%d7%9e%d7%99%d7%a0%d7%99%d7%9e%d7%95%d7%9d.aspx
--     14:52:49Z, sha256 0c7ff9205881f9b13396791c2b058bb511b1ec2e51bd6a9cb9ae20effa5ac743
@ref National Insurance Institute, "minimum wage", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); Schedule K "שכר מינימום" (source line 4772)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2025, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 6_247.67

@ref National Insurance Institute, "minimum wage", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); Schedule K "שכר מינימום" (source line 4772)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly minimum wage for an employee aged 18 or over from 1 April 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 6_443.85
